## 🧠 My Analysis

The **54/71 detection rate** gave me a high level of confidence that the file should be treated as malicious.

I looked at the overall pattern instead of relying on a single antivirus result. Multiple security vendors independently classified the file as malicious, with several identifying it as a Trojan or backdoor.

The repeated **FlagPro** and **Fragtor** family labels also provided additional context about the type of malware associated with the file.

Based on these findings, I would treat the file as a **malicious artifact** and continue investigating the affected system if this were a real SOC incident.

